course: dictionary
lesson: 9735
title: Sunni
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Sunni is a word about Islam, one of the world's big religions. Islam has two main branches, or groups: Sunni and Shia. A Sunni is a Muslim who belongs to the Sunni branch, and «Sunni Muslims» means Muslims from that branch.
explain: Sunni and Shia Muslims share the same core beliefs: one God, the Prophet Muhammad, the Qur'an and the Five Pillars. They disagree about one main question: who should have led Muslims after the Prophet Muhammad died.
explain: Context helps you work out the word. «The Safavid dynasty made Shia Islam the state religion, while their Ottoman neighbours and rivals were Sunni Muslims.» The word «while» shows a contrast: one group was Shia, and the other group was Sunni. So Sunni names a different branch.
explain: Words can change their job in a sentence. In «Sunni mosques», Sunni describes the mosques, so it is an adjective. Always speak about Sunni, Shia and other faiths with respect.
fact: Sunni is the largest branch of Islam.
fact: Most Muslims in the world are Sunni.
fact: A Sunni is a Muslim who belongs to the Sunni branch.
fact: Sunni and Shia Muslims share core beliefs, but disagree about who should have led Muslims after the Prophet Muhammad died.
fact: «Sunni and Shia» are the two main branches of Islam, so they are often mentioned together.
exercise: What is the largest branch of Islam? | *Sunni | Hindu | Shia | Catholic
exercise: «The Safavid dynasty made Shia Islam the state religion, while their Ottoman neighbours and rivals were Sunni Muslims.» Which word shows the two groups were different? | Safavid | Persia | *while | finest
exercise: Sunni and Shia Muslims share core beliefs but disagree about what? | *Who should have led Muslims after the Prophet Muhammad died | Which country to live in | The colour of the Qur'an | What to eat for breakfast
test: In «Sunni mosques», what kind of word is Sunni? | *adjective | adverb | noun | verb
test: What do Sunni and Shia Muslims share? | Only the same prayers at the same time each day | Different holy books | *One God, the Prophet Muhammad, the Qur'an and the Five Pillars | Nothing at all
exam: Which statement is true? | *Most Muslims in the world are Sunni | Most Muslims in the world are Shia | Sunni is a type of food | Sunni is a country
